{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception capabilities, separating motion commands from sensor events. The specification encodes a deterministic exploration policy: random_walk is preferred in clear states for coverage, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery is conservative and minimal. Obstacle events force recovery turns; only after path_clear does the robot resume exploration. Full_rotate is used only after repeated obstacles. All uncontrollable events are handled in every state, and only one controllable is enabled per state to avoid oscillation.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to reflect hardware modularity.",
    "Specification automaton encodes a deterministic exploration policy with conservative recovery, prioritizing random_walk and move_forward in clear states and using rotate_clockwise/counterclockwise for obstacle recovery."
